<DocsLayout
  title="Alerts & widgets"
  description="Create ilyStream browser-source widgets, live alert routes, media assets, platform filters, and test events."
  slug="alerts-widgets"
  updated="July 2026"
  readingTime="10 min"
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>
    ilyStream has two overlay layers. Widgets are persistent browser sources like
    Unified Chat, Now Playing, goals, and screen borders. Alert routes are event
    reactions that fire when something happens, such as a follow, gift, sub, raid,
    chat keyword, or join.
  </p>

  <h2 id="widgets">Widgets</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open Create &rarr; Overlays &amp; Widgets.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Click New Widget.</strong> Pick Unified Chat, Event Alerts, Follower Goal, Goal Tracker, Now Playing, Socials Rotation, or Screen Border.</li>
    <li><strong>Copy the browser-source URL.</strong> Each widget card has a local URL that can be pasted into OBS or another browser-source tool.</li>
    <li><strong>Configure the widget.</strong> Use the Configure button to change layout, colors, labels, and widget-specific behavior.</li>
    <li><strong>Use the open button to inspect it.</strong> Open the widget in a browser when you want a full-size preview.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="alert-routes">Alert routes</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Open Create &rarr; Alert Routes.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Create or select a route.</strong> Routes can be broad, like all follows, or very specific, like Twitch raids only.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose platforms.</strong> Use All or select TikTok, Twitch, YouTube, or Kick.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose events.</strong> Pick chat, gift, sub/member, follow, raid, like, share, or join.</li>
    <li><strong>Add optional keyword filters.</strong> Use this when a route should only fire on a specific phrase.</li>
    <li><strong>Set outputs.</strong> Configure sound, image, text, and style tabs as needed.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="assets">Assets</h2>
  <p>
    Alert routes can use sounds and images stored in ilyStream. Keep assets short,
    stream-safe, and easy to recognize.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sounds</strong>: short <code>.wav</code> or <code>.mp3</code> files work best.</li>
    <li><strong>Images</strong>: transparent <code>.png</code> files are easiest to place over gameplay.</li>
    <li><strong>Names</strong>: use names you can recognize in a hurry, such as <code>follow-soft-chime</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Volume</strong>: adjust route gain instead of editing the audio file every time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="obs">OBS and TikTok Studio</h2>
  <p>
    OBS browser sources and TikTok Live Studio browser sources can both use
    ilyStream URLs. Keep ilyStream open while streaming so the local overlay server
    stays available.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Copy the widget URL.</strong> Use the copy icon on the widget card.</li>
    <li><strong>Add a Browser Source.</strong> Paste the URL into OBS or TikTok Live Studio.</li>
    <li><strong>Use the correct canvas size.</strong> Set 1920x1080 for horizontal overlays or the vertical size shown by the app for mobile layouts.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep transparency.</strong> If a source shows black, set the browser source background CSS to transparent.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="testing">Testing</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Use Test alert.</strong> Fire the selected route without waiting for a real viewer event.</li>
    <li><strong>Watch the live preview.</strong> Confirm image, text, sound, and timing are correct.</li>
    <li><strong>Use Event Testing for broader checks.</strong> Fire synthetic follows, chats, gifts, and overlay events before going live.</li>
    <li><strong>Re-check audio.</strong> If local alert sounds are on, avoid also monitoring the OBS browser source audio unless you want double playback.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
  <p><strong>The widget is blank in OBS.</strong> Open the URL in a normal browser. If it does not load, ilyStream or the overlay server is not running.</p>
  <p><strong>The alert fires twice.</strong> Check whether the route is duplicated or whether both ilyStream and OBS are monitoring the same alert audio.</p>
  <p><strong>A route fires for the wrong platform.</strong> Clear All, select the exact platform, and test again.</p>
  <p><strong>The text is clipped.</strong> Reduce font size or increase the widget/source dimensions. Fixed-size browser sources will crop oversized alert text.</p>

